WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.073
Give your clients a choice on one quote.

00:00:03.073 --> 00:00:07.400
Here's how to offer Good, Better, and Best options in Worklio Pro.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.996
Start a new quote, or open one you've already made.

00:00:11.996 --> 00:00:14.925
In Product and Service, click Offer options.

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:20.890
Name each option, like Repair, Replace, and Replace with high efficiency.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:27.025
Add what's included if you like, and mark one as recommended, so it stands out to your client.

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:31.821
Next, add your line items and set each one's option.

00:00:31.821 --> 00:00:37.700
Items like a diagnostic visit can go in All options, so they're part of every choice.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.617
Each option's total updates as you go.

00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:46.550
Discount, tax, and any deposit apply to the option your client picks.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.725
Save the quote, and send it the usual way.

00:00:51.925 --> 00:00:57.190
Your client sees every option side by side, with an Approve button for each one.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:02.850
They pick the one they want, then sign and pay any deposit, just like any other quote.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:08.875
You're told which option they chose, and the quote now shows only their choice.

00:01:10.075 --> 00:01:17.400
If a client tells you their choice in person, open the quote, choose Mark as Approved, and pick the option they want.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.617
It all works on your phone too.

00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:24.975
Line items are grouped by option, with a button to add to each one.

00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:33.550
When you convert the quote to a job, only the chosen option's items carry over, ready to schedule and invoice.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.341
That's Good, Better, Best.

00:01:36.341 --> 00:01:39.400
You'll find this guide anytime in the Help Center.
